        "original_id": "c86f7f9a-95e0-5b3f-ba28-a7923b83a154",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Manru\n- People: Ignacy Jan Paderewski, Alfred Nossig, Henry Edward Krehbiel, Józef Ignacy Kraszewski\n- Topics: opera, libretto, Polish independence\n\nFacts:\n- In 1843, Józef Ignacy Kraszewski published the novel \"A Hut Behind the Village,\" which later became the basis for the opera Manru.\n- Ignacy Jan Paderewski was born on 18 November 1860 and became a Polish pianist, composer, politician, and spokesman for Polish independence.\n- Manru is a three-act opera described as a lyrical drama, with music composed by Ignacy Jan Paderewski.\n- Alfred Nossig wrote the libretto for Manru, and Henry Edward Krehbiel produced its English translation.\n- Ignacy Jan Paderewski died on 29 June 1941.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
